{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792412040,"nonce":"3uZsCLCkqXJdUdPCJZ6GaWomYZY=","title":"TAST name resolution scans the whole symbol table for each call","message":"Frame-pointer profile, nue `examples/llama-chat/Main.hx` typecheck (2026-10-19), share of lower_to_tast:\n- `AstLowering::resolve_class_method_symbol`: 48%. Strategies 2, 2b and 4 call `find_symbols` over every symbol, filtering by `name == method_name` and then by qualified name.\n- `resolve_callee_formal_param_types`: 29%.\n- `resolve_class_like_symbol_by_name`: 10%.\n\nThat is quadratic in program size, and it slows every CLI compile as well as the LSP.\n\nA name index (simple name -\u003e symbol ids) on SymbolTable would make these scans of a few same-named symbols. Names change after insertion only through the BLADE manifest renames (manifest.rs `sym.name = short_name`, five sites), which would need a `SymbolTable::rename` that updates the index. Lookups verify `sym.name` so a stale entry cannot match.\n\nThe BLADE manifest load's per-method scan has already been replaced with a per-load qualified-name map (register_symbols_from_manifest).","files":null}]}